                    },
                    "message": "I did additional testing in simulation based on your comment and some changes I made in patch set 2."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/src/gpios_only_device.hpp",
                    "line": 79,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I can't find a release() in the gpio_line destructor. Will the GPIO get implicitly released in the kernel when this app goes away?  Or am I missing a release() somewhere else in your code for this GPIO?  If not, it should probably go in the destructor."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-power-sequencer/src/gpios_only_device.hpp",
                    "line": 79,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Good question.\n\nThe GPIO object contains a gpiod::line. The gpiod::line destructor releases the line. So this will happen automatically. I tested this to confirm.\n\nHowever, I'll add a comment to document this."
                }
            ],
